From e18fc842c047113866334521e0668ad023e20599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junior Mverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:48:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: also limit the WSA MIX path digital
 volumes

The WSA macro exposes WSA_RX0_MIX and WSA_RX1_MIX Digital Volume controls
with the same -84..+40 dB range as the main paths. The speaker volume
limit in the machine driver covers only WSA_RX0 and WSA_RX1, so the MIX
controls keep their full range and their 0 dB register default, which is
above the -3 dB ceiling used for the main path.

Apply the same ceiling to the MIX controls of both macro instances until
speaker protection is available.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
index c81df41ac..78606fcae 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/x1e80100.c
@@ -43,6 +43,11 @@ static int x1e80100_snd_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA WSA_RX1 Digital Volume", 81);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA2 WSA_RX0 Digital Volume", 81);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA2 WSA_RX1 Digital Volume", 81);
+		/* The MIX paths feed the same amplifier; do not leave them at +40 dB */
+		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA WSA_RX0_MIX Digital Volume", 81);
+		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA WSA_RX1_MIX Digital Volume", 81);
+		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA2 WSA_RX0_MIX Digital Volume", 81);
+		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WSA2 WSA_RX1_MIX Digital Volume", 81);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrLeft PA Volume", 6);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "SpkrRight PA Volume", 6);
 		snd_soc_limit_volume(card, "WooferLeft PA Volume", 6);
